# Events on the vineyard roads (data/random_encounters/vineyard_road.json).

~ keepers_word
if flag.raven_word_heard
-> END
endif
set raven_word_heard
Narrator: A raven lands on the road ahead, drops something at your feet and waits. It's a vine leaf, fresh and green, the first leaf you've seen in this valley that isn't half dead.
if flag.winery_wine_flows
Narrator: It caws twice, briskly, like a man clearing his throat to say thank you, and flies off toward the vineyards.
elif flag.winery_reclaimed
Narrator: It looks at the leaf, then west toward Yester Hill, then at you, with great meaning, and goes.
else
Narrator: It looks at the leaf, then toward the vineyards south of the lake road, then back at you, as if you were being slow on purpose.
endif
if name:godrick_pendlebrook
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: I think that was a letter. From a bird. Do we write back?
else
interject tag:curious: I think we just got a letter.
endif
-> END

